      "text": [
        " : \"أَرْبَعٌ يَذْهَبْنَ ضَيَاعاً مَوَدَّةٌ تُمْنَحُ مَنْ لاَ وَفَاءَ لَهُ وَ مَعْرُوفٌ يُوضَعُ عِنْدَ مَنْ لاَ يَشْكُرُهُ وَ عِلْمٌ يُعَلَّمُ مَنْ لاَ يَسْتَمِعُ لَهُ وَ سِرٌّ يُودَعُ مَنْ لاَ حَضَانَةَ لَهُ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5907 - It is narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Isa, from Ali ibn Ismail, from Abdullah ibn Al-Waleed, from Abu Basir, from Abu Abdullah Al-Sadiq Ja'far ibn Muhammad (as), who said: \"Four things are wasted in vain:\nAffection granted to one who has no loyalty,\nA favor bestowed upon one who does not appreciate it,\nKnowledge taught to one who does not listen,\nAnd a secret entrusted to one who has no sense of safeguarding.\""
        ]
      }
